istance":0.6045,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"CAR","distance":0.676,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2021,"team":"JAX","distance":0.6935,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2018,"team":"MIA","distance":0.7227,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2019,"team":"CIN","distance":0.7669,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Lions went 12-5 in 2023 and outscored opponents 461 to 395. The offense carried the team, ranking 7th in EPA per play while the defense finished 17th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive traits were the 2nd lowest shotgun rate and the 2nd highest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Lions had one of the most efficient offenses in the league, ranking in the top eight in all five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Their biggest outliers in how they lined up were the 2nd lowest shotgun rate and the 3rd highest under center rate in the league. Jared Goff ran the passing game and leaned heavily on Amon-Ra St. Brown, who drew 29% of the targets.","defense":"The Lions defense was about average by EPA allowed per play. It was much better against the run than the pass, ranking 3rd and 22nd. Aidan Hutchinson was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Alim McNeill, who had 5 sacks, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. In terms of scheme, they had the 2nd highest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Lions were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 90% of field goals, which was a little above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the offensive line, about 24% of the money on the books.","players":"Jared Goff played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 4,575 yards. Amon-Ra St. Brown was the clear top target with 29% of the looks and 1,515 receiving yards. The backfield was a committee led by David Montgomery and Jahmyr Gibbs. On defense, Aidan Hutchinson led the team with 11.5 sacks and Kerby Joseph picked off 4 passes.","coaching":"Ben Johnson called the offense and Aaron Glenn called the defense. Their offense looked most like the 2025 Bears under Ben Johnson and the 2022 Cowboys under Kellen Moore. Their defense looked most like the 2021 and 2022 Panthers.","trends":"The offense went from 6th in EPA per play in 2022 to 7th in 2023, about where it was. The defense moved from 30th in EPA allowed per play in 2022 to 17th in 2023, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was Cover 4 rate, which went from 6% to 14%.","notes":"Every data source is available for 2023. This season uses the newer formation labels, which group singleback, I formation and empty sets together as under center, so those older formation rates are not shown."}}